# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep secrets and runtime
# state out of it. A `.env` or a SQLite file in the build context risks being
# copied into an intermediate layer even when a later `COPY` does not mention
# it — layers are addressed independently, so anything sent to the daemon can be
# recovered from the cache.

.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Rebuilt inside the image.
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# Never ship a developer's database or uploads into an image.
storage
**/storage
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Tests are not needed to run the server and would give anyone who can pull
# the image a copy of the acceptance harness.
**/test
**/*.test.ts
packages/core/test
apps/api/test

openapi.json
*.log
docs/**/*.png
README.md
